        "original_id": "10dea670-5b85-51c5-be7e-1cdc4ae669da",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Abdelghani Bousta\n- Places: Marrakesh, Morocco, Paris, Père-Lachaise cemetery\n- Roles: Moroccan politician\n- Topics: Moroccan monarchy, city size in Morocco\n\nFacts:\n- Abdelghani Bousta was born on 18 February 1949 in Marrakesh, Morocco.\n- Marrakesh is a major city of the Kingdom of Morocco.\n- Marrakesh is the fourth largest city in Morocco, after Casablanca, Fez, and Tangier.\n- Abdelghani Bousta was a Moroccan politician who opposed the monarchical power of Morocco.\n- Abdelghani Bousta died on 21 September 1998 and was buried at Père-Lachaise cemetery in Paris, France.",
